.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt PKG6DEPOTD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg6depotd
.Nd IPS repository depot server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /usr/lib/pkg6depotd
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Op Fl -repository-root Ar directory
.Op Fl -bind Ar ip:port
.Op Cm start | Cm config-test
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon serves an IPS package repository to
.Xr pkg 1
clients over the pkg5 depot protocol.
It is normally run by the
.Xr smf 7
service
.Sy svc:/application/pkg/pkg6depotd
and not invoked directly.
.Pp
By default the depot speaks plain HTTP and is meant to run behind a reverse
proxy that terminates TLS.
It can also serve HTTPS itself, with a certificate from files or one
obtained and renewed through ACME; see
.Sx TLS .
.Pp
The public HTTP interface is read-only.
Repositories are created and changed with the local
.Nm pkg6repo
command.
.Pp
The following options are supported:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar file , Fl -config Ar file
Read the KDL configuration from
.Ar file .
.It Fl -repository-root Ar directory
Override the repository root in the KDL file with an absolute path.
The SMF method supplies this option from
.Sy pkg/inst_root .
.It Fl -bind Ar ip:port
Override the KDL listener with one IP address and port.
The SMF method supplies this option from
.Sy pkg/address
and
.Sy pkg/port .
An IPv6 address must be bracketed in this command-line value.
.It Fl -tls-cert-file Ar file , Fl -tls-key-file Ar file
Serve TLS from an absolute PEM certificate chain and private key.
Give both options or neither.
They replace the KDL
.Sy tls
certificate, key and
.Sy acme
settings; the KDL
.Sy handshake-timeout
still applies.
The SMF method supplies them from
.Sy pkg/ssl_cert_file
and
.Sy pkg/ssl_key_file .
.El
.Pp
.Nm
always runs in the foreground; SMF supervises it.
There is no daemon mode, pid file or control command: stop the depot with
.Dv SIGTERM ,
for example through
.Nm svcadm disable ,
and reload its TLS certificate with
.Dv SIGHUP ,
for example through
.Nm svcadm refresh .
The option
.Fl -no-daemon
of earlier releases is accepted and ignored.
.Pp
The following commands are supported:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm start
Serve the repository.
This is the default.
.It Cm config-test
Load and validate the configuration and print a summary: the file, the bind
address, the repository root and the TLS mode.
With certificate files, the certificate and key are loaded and checked;
with ACME, the permissions of the DNS API token file and of the state
directory are checked.
Other settings are not printed, because they may hold credentials.
Exits non-zero if the file is missing or invalid, including invalid
.Sx TELEMETRY
or
.Sx TLS
settings.
Error messages give the line and column of a problem, not the offending text.
The repository is not opened and no ACME request is made.
.El
.Pp
On
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT ,
.Nm
stops accepting connections, gives running requests up to 10 seconds to
finish, then flushes telemetry within
.Sy shutdown-timeout-ms
and exits.
.Sh TELEMETRY
Local log output goes to standard output, which SMF writes to the service
log.
The
.Sy telemetry
block of the configuration file controls it and the optional export of
traces, metrics and logs to an OpenTelemetry collector over OTLP/HTTP
(protobuf):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
telemetry {
    service-name "pkg6depotd"
    log-format "json"
    otlp {
        enabled true
        endpoint "http://127.0.0.1:4318"
    }
}
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy service-name
The
.Sy service.name
resource attribute.
Default
.Sy pkg6depotd .
.It Sy log-format
.Sy text
(default) or
.Sy json
for the local log output.
.El
.Pp
Earlier configurations may carry a top-level
.Sy otlp-endpoint
key inside
.Sy telemetry .
It never enabled export and is now rejected at load time: move the URL to
.Sy endpoint
in the
.Sy otlp
block and set
.Sy enabled
as wanted.
.Pp
Keys of the
.Sy otlp
block:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy enabled
.Sy true
or
.Sy false .
Defaults to
.Sy true
when the block is present.
Other keys are validated even when export is disabled.
.It Sy endpoint
Base URL of the collector's OTLP/HTTP receiver, such as
.Pa http://127.0.0.1:4318 .
The paths
.Pa /v1/traces ,
.Pa /v1/metrics
and
.Pa /v1/logs
are appended.
Required when enabled.
Only
.Sy http
and
.Sy https
URLs without user credentials, query or fragment are accepted; the URL is
never repeated in error messages.
To authenticate to a remote collector, run a local collector that adds the
credentials.
Export connects to this URL directly:
.Ev HTTP_PROXY ,
.Ev HTTPS_PROXY
and
.Ev ALL_PROXY
in the service environment are ignored and redirects are not followed.
.It Sy traces , metrics , logs
Export the signal:
.Sy true
(default) or
.Sy false .
At least one must be enabled.
.It Sy log-level
Minimum level of exported log records:
.Sy error , warn , info
(default),
.Sy debug
or
.Sy trace .
The local output keeps using
.Sy config/log_filter .
.It Sy sample-ratio
Fraction of requests traced, 0.0 to 1.0.
Default 1.0.
.It Sy timeout-ms
Limit for one export attempt, 50 to 60000.
Default 5000.
.It Sy max-retries
Retries of a failed export, with exponential backoff from 100 ms up to 5 s,
0 to 10.
Default 3.
A batch that still fails is dropped.
A 4xx answer other than 408 and 429 means the collector rejected the payload;
it is dropped without retrying.
.It Sy queue-size
Trace spans and log records buffered per signal, 1 to 65536.
Default 2048.
When the queue is full the oldest record is dropped.
.It Sy batch-size
Records per export request, 1 to 8192 and at most
.Sy queue-size .
Default 512.
.It Sy flush-interval-ms
Longest time a span or log record waits before it is sent, 10 to 60000.
Default 5000.
.It Sy metrics-interval-ms
Metrics export interval, 100 to 3600000.
Default 60000.
.It Sy shutdown-timeout-ms
Time allowed to flush telemetry when the service stops, 100 to 30000.
Default 5000.
Records still queued afterwards are dropped.
.El
.Pp
Export runs on its own threads and never delays requests.
A slow, hung or unreachable collector costs at most
.Sy queue-size
queued records plus the one batch of up to
.Sy batch-size
records being sent, per signal, of memory; dropped records are counted by
signal and by
reason
.Po
.Sy overflow ,
.Sy export_failed ,
.Sy shutdown
.Pc
in the
.Sy pkg6depotd.telemetry.dropped
metric.
.Pp
Metrics:
.Sy pkg6depotd.http.server.requests ,
.Sy http.server.request.duration ,
.Sy http.server.active_requests ,
.Sy pkg6depotd.http.server.errors
(5xx responses),
.Sy pkg6depotd.operations ,
.Sy pkg6depotd.operation.duration ,
.Sy pkg6depotd.telemetry.dropped
and
.Sy pkg6depotd.telemetry.exported .
The two operation metrics are reserved for repository imports, catalog
rebuilds and retirements; this release does not record them yet.
Each request produces one server span.
Attributes are limited to the HTTP method, the route template (for example
.Pa /{publisher}/file/1/{digest} ,
or
.Sy unmatched ) ,
the status code, the operation and the result; request paths, package names
and digests are never attributes.
Exported log records carry the message text, which can name packages.
.Sh SERVICE
The service runs as the
.Sy pkg6srv
user and group with the privileges
.Sy basic ,
.Sy net_privaddr ,
less
.Sy file_link_any ,
.Sy proc_info
and
.Sy proc_session .
It can therefore bind ports below 1024.
.Pp
The default instance is delivered disabled.
The package does not create the repository location, so removing the
package never touches repository data.
Before enabling the service, create it, preferably as its own ZFS dataset,
create the repository as the service user and review the configuration file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zfs create -o mountpoint=/var/pkg6depotd rpool/pkg6depotd
# chown pkg6srv:pkg6srv /var/pkg6depotd
# chmod 0750 /var/pkg6depotd
# su pkg6srv -c '/usr/bin/pkg6repo create /var/pkg6depotd/repo'
# su pkg6srv -c '/usr/bin/pkg6repo add-publisher \e
      -s /var/pkg6depotd/repo openindiana.org'
# svcadm enable pkg6depotd
.Ed
.Pp
While it serves a repository managed through generations, the depot
records package accesses for retirement in
.Pa retention/access/
below the repository, which it creates itself.
Run
.Xr pkg6repo 1
and
.Xr pkg6repo-retire 8
commands against the repository as
.Sy pkg6srv
too, so that every file there stays writable by the depot.
.Pp
The service is configured with the following properties:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy config/file
Path of the configuration file.
The default is
.Pa /etc/pkg6depotd/pkg6depotd.kdl .
The service will not start if the file is missing, unreadable by
.Sy pkg6srv ,
or invalid; there are no built-in defaults.
The start method runs
.Cm config-test
on the file first and, if it fails, puts the instance into maintenance;
fix the file, then run
.Nm svcadm clear .
.It Sy config/log_filter
A
.Ev RUST_LOG
filter such as
.Sy info
or
.Sy pkg6depotd=debug .
Empty selects the built-in default.
.It Sy pkg/inst_root
Absolute path to the repository served by this instance.
Set it together with
.Sy pkg/port ;
an empty value leaves the KDL repository path in effect.
.It Sy pkg/port
TCP port served by this instance, from 1 through 65535.
Set it together with
.Sy pkg/inst_root ;
zero leaves the KDL bind address in effect.
.It Sy pkg/address
IP address for this instance.
When
.Sy pkg/port
is set and this property is empty, the depot binds to
.Li 127.0.0.1 .
Use an unbracketed IPv6 address such as
.Li ::1 .
.It Sy pkg/ssl_cert_file , pkg/ssl_key_file
Absolute paths to a PEM TLS certificate chain and private key.
Set both or leave both empty; setting only one puts the instance in
maintenance.
When set, they replace the KDL
.Sy tls
certificate, key and
.Sy acme
settings, and work whether or not
.Sy pkg/inst_root
and
.Sy pkg/port
are set.
Empty values leave the KDL TLS settings in effect.
The files must be readable by
.Sy pkg6srv ;
the private key must not be readable by other users.
.El
.Pp
These property groups are defined on the service, not on the
.Sy default
instance.
Set them on the service, then refresh and restart the instance:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# svccfg -s pkg6depotd setprop config/log_filter = astring: debug
# svcadm refresh pkg6depotd:default
# svcadm restart pkg6depotd:default
.Ed
.Pp
Running
.Nm svccfg Fl s Sy pkg6depotd:default Cm setprop
fails with
.Dq \&No such property group ,
because the instance has no
.Sy config
property group of its own.
.Pp
Configuration file changes take effect on
.Nm svcadm restart .
.Nm svcadm refresh
sends
.Dv SIGHUP ,
which only re-reads the TLS certificate and key.
Diagnostic output goes to the SMF log shown by
.Nm svcs Fl L Sy pkg6depotd .
.Pp
Several depots can run side by side as separate instances, as with
.Sy svc:/application/pkg/server .
Give each additional instance a
.Sy pkg
property group with its own repository path and listener.
An instance may also override
.Sy config/file
with its own
.Sy config
property group when it needs KDL settings of its own, such as ACME or
telemetry:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# svccfg -s pkg6depotd add legacy
# svccfg -s pkg6depotd:legacy addpg pkg application
# svccfg -s pkg6depotd:legacy setprop pkg/inst_root = \e
      astring: /var/pkg6depotd/legacy
# svccfg -s pkg6depotd:legacy setprop pkg/port = count: 8081
# svccfg -s pkg6depotd:legacy setprop pkg/address = \e
      astring: 127.0.0.1
# svcadm refresh pkg6depotd:legacy
# svcadm enable pkg6depotd:legacy
.Ed
.Pp
The repository must exist and be readable by
.Sy pkg6srv
before enabling the instance.
The depot validates the resulting KDL and SMF values before it starts;
an incomplete
.Sy pkg/inst_root
and
.Sy pkg/port
pair puts the instance into maintenance.
Changes to these properties require
.Nm svcadm restart .
Package upgrades restart all running instances, and package removal
disables all instances.
.Sh TLS
Without a
.Ic tls
block the depot serves plain HTTP on
.Ic server.bind .
Keep that address private to the reverse proxy.
.Pp
With a
.Ic tls
block the depot serves HTTPS only.
TLS 1.2 and 1.3 are offered, with HTTP/1.1.
The configuration is checked strictly: a
.Ic tls
block that names no certificate source, names both sources, or is
otherwise inconsistent is an error, and so is the obsolete
.Ic server.tls-cert
setting.
The depot never falls back to plain HTTP, and it opens the HTTPS port only
after it holds a valid certificate.
.Ss Certificate files
.Bd -literal -offset indent
tls {
    certificate "/etc/pkg6depotd/tls/fullchain.pem"
    key "/etc/pkg6depotd/tls/key.pem"
}
.Ed
.Pp
.Ic certificate
holds the PEM certificate chain, leaf first;
.Ic key
holds the matching PEM private key.
Both are read by
.Sy pkg6srv ;
the key file must not be readable by other users, so use owner
.Sy root ,
group
.Sy pkg6srv
and mode 0640.
The service does not start if either is unreadable, if the key file is
accessible to other users, if the key does not match the certificate, or
if the certificate has expired or is not valid yet.
.Cm config-test
applies the same checks.
After installing a renewed pair, run
.Nm svcadm refresh Sy pkg6depotd .
New connections then use the new certificate.
If the new files fail any of these checks, an error is logged and the old
certificate stays in service.
.Ss ACME
.Bd -literal -offset indent
tls {
    acme {
        domains "pkg.example.org"
        contact "mailto:hostmaster@example.org"
        terms-agreed true
        staging true
        state-dir "/var/pkg6depotd/acme"
        challenge "http-01"
        http01-bind "0.0.0.0:80"
    }
}
.Ed
.Pp
The following settings are supported in the
.Ic acme
block:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic domains Ar name ...
The DNS names of the certificate, at most 100.
Wildcards such as
.Sy *.example.org
require dns-01.
.It Ic contact Ar mailto:address ...
Addresses the CA may use for expiry and policy notices.
Optional.
.It Ic terms-agreed Sy true
Required.
States that the operator accepts the CA's subscriber agreement.
.It Ic staging Sy true
Use the Let's Encrypt staging CA.
Its certificates are not trusted by clients, but its rate limits allow
testing.
Remove it once issuance works.
.It Ic directory-url Ar url
The ACME directory of another CA.
It must be an https URL.
Every URL the CA returns must be https as well, and orders and
authorizations must be for exactly the configured
.Ic domains ;
anything else is refused before a challenge is answered.
The default is the Let's Encrypt production CA.
.It Ic state-dir Ar dir
Required.
Holds the account key, an order in progress and the certificate.
The depot creates the directory with mode 0700 if its parent is writable
by
.Sy pkg6srv ;
it refuses to start if the directory is accessible to other users or
owned by another user.
.It Ic renew-before-days Ar days
Renew this many days before expiry, 1 to 60, default 30.
Certificates are renewed at the latest when a third of their lifetime
is left.
.It Ic challenge Sy http-01 | Sy dns-01
Required.
With
.Sy http-01 ,
the CA fetches a token from
.Pa http://domain/.well-known/acme-challenge/ ;
.Ic http01-bind
names the plain HTTP listener that answers it, usually
.Sy 0.0.0.0:80 .
Port 80 of every domain must reach that listener.
It answers only challenge tokens and redirects other requests for the
configured domains to HTTPS on the port of
.Ic server.bind .
With
.Sy dns-01 ,
the depot creates
.Sy _acme-challenge
TXT records through the provider's API, as configured in a
.Ic dns01
block.
.El
.Pp
The
.Ic dns01
block takes:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic provider Sy cloudflare | Sy gandi
The DNS provider.
Cloudflare needs an API token with Zone.DNS edit rights on the zone.
Challenge records carry the comment
.Qq pkg6depotd ACME dns-01 challenge
and are only deleted when name, value and comment all match.
Gandi needs a personal access token with LiveDNS rights.
The depot adds and removes only its own values in the
.Sy _acme-challenge
TXT record set and never replaces or deletes the whole set, so other TXT
values at that name are kept.
.It Ic api-token-file Ar file
A file holding only the token.
It must not be readable by other users; use owner
.Sy root ,
group
.Sy pkg6srv
and mode 0640.
The token itself never appears in the configuration, in
.Cm config-test
output or in log messages.
.It Ic zone Ar name
The DNS zone that contains all
.Ic domains .
.It Ic zone-id Ar id
Cloudflare only: the zone identifier, which skips a lookup by name.
.It Ic propagation-seconds Ar seconds
How long to wait after creating the records before the CA checks them,
0 to 3600, default 60.
.It Ic ttl Ar seconds
TTL of the TXT records: 60 to 86400 for Cloudflare, default 120;
300 to 2592000 for Gandi, default 300.
.El
.Pp
At startup the depot uses the stored certificate if it is currently valid.
Otherwise it makes up to three attempts to obtain one, 10 seconds apart,
and exits with an error if they all fail.
Failed attempts are counted in the state directory, so a restarted depot
does not start over: it waits 5 minutes before its next attempt, then 10,
20 and so on, up to six hours, without opening the HTTPS port meanwhile.
The service therefore stays online but does not serve until issuance
succeeds; check the log.
Remove
.Pa backoff.json
from the state directory to retry at once; changing
.Ic domains
or the CA also starts afresh.
While running, the depot renews the certificate in the background and
installs the new one without a restart.
A failed renewal is logged and retried on the same schedule, while the
current certificate stays in service.
Every request to the CA and to the DNS provider has a timeout, and polling
is bounded.
Challenge tokens and DNS records are removed after every attempt.
DNS records are listed in
.Pa challenges.json
before they are created.
If the depot is stopped or crashes while records exist, they are removed
at its next start, or before its next issuance; until then they stay at
the provider.
http-01 tokens are only held in memory and end with the process.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/pkg6depotd/pkg6depotd.kdl
Default configuration.
It is readable by root and the
.Sy pkg6srv
group only.
Package upgrades keep an edited copy and install the new default as
.Pa pkg6depotd.kdl.new .
.It Pa /var/pkg6depotd
Default location of repositories.
Created by the administrator, not by the package.
.It Pa /var/pkg6depotd/acme
Suggested ACME state directory.
Not delivered by the package; create it owned by
.Sy pkg6srv
with mode 0700:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# mkdir -m 0700 /var/pkg6depotd/acme
# chown pkg6srv:pkg6srv /var/pkg6depotd/acme
.Ed
.Pp
Keep it across upgrades and in backups.
.Pa certificate.pem
holds the private key and certificate chain and is replaced atomically;
.Pa account-*.json
holds one account key per ACME directory;
.Pa order.json
exists only while an order is in progress;
.Pa challenges.json
lists dns-01 records that may still exist at the provider;
if it is damaged the depot refuses to issue and does not overwrite it:
remove the listed records at the provider, then delete the file;
.Pa backoff.json
counts failed issuance attempts.
All files are mode 0600.
.It Pa /lib/svc/manifest/application/pkg/pkg6depotd.xml
SMF service manifest.
.It Pa /lib/svc/method/svc-pkg6depotd
SMF start method.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The following exit values are returned:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy 0
.Cm start :
the depot stopped after a signal.
.Cm config-test :
the configuration is valid.
.It Sy 1
The configuration is missing or invalid, or the depot could not start or
failed while serving.
.It Sy 2
Invalid command line, including an unknown command.
.El
.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
.Sy Uncommitted
